# auth.md

You are an agent. Elliot supports **agentic registration** ([auth.md](https://github.com/workos/auth.md)) with one method, `service_auth`: register with your person's email, they sign in to Elliot and type a 6-digit code you give them, then you collect an API key. The key acts as your person in one Elliot workspace, on the MCP server and the REST API.

Elliot finds exploitable vulnerabilities in GitHub repositories and files each one as a finding on the team's board. People read about it at https://www.tryelliot.app.

## Rules

- Register only for the person you work for, when they ask, with their own email address.
- The code goes from you to your person. They type it into the Elliot page they open; they give it to nobody else.
- The API key is a credential. Keep it where your person says, out of repositories, logs and command arguments.
- Before you register, tell your person the key starts with a $0 spend cap, which only they can raise (Spend cap, below).
- Read prices from https://www.tryelliot.app/pricing.md. Quote none from memory.

## Step 1: Discover

The API answers a call with no key with a 401 that points at its resource metadata:

```http
GET https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/v1/me

HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
WWW-Authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata="https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/v1"
```

- Protected resource metadata: https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/api/v1
- Authorization server metadata, with the `agent_auth` block: https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server

In `agent_auth`: `identity_endpoint` is https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/agent/identity, `claim_endpoint` is https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/agent/identity/claim, and `identity_types_supported` is `["service_auth"]`. The `token_endpoint` at the top level answers the claim grant.

## Step 2: Register

```sh
curl -sS -X POST https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/agent/identity \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"type": "service_auth", "login_hint": "maya@yourcompany.com", "agent_name": "Claude Code"}'
```

`agent_name` is how Elliot labels you on the claim page and the Agents page. `scope` is optional, space-separated, from `findings:read findings:write scans:run` (all three by default; `findings:read` always).

Response (200):

```json
{
  "registration_id": "reg_…",
  "registration_type": "service_auth",
  "claim_url": "https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/agent/identity/claim",
  "claim_token": "clm_…",
  "claim_token_expires": "2026-11-18T19:00:00.000Z",
  "post_claim_scopes": ["findings:read", "findings:write", "scans:run"],
  "claim": {
    "user_code": "123456",
    "expires_in": 600,
    "verification_uri": "https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/agent/claim?t=cla_…",
    "interval": 5
  },
  "limits": {"spend": {"cap": {"currency": "USD", "value": "0.00"}, "spent": {"currency": "USD", "value": "0.00"}, "period": "total", "resets_at": null}}
}
```

The answer is the same whether or not the address already has an Elliot account. Hold `claim_token` in memory until Step 4.

## Step 3: Hand off to your person

Send them the link and the code in one message:

> Open this link, sign in to Elliot (or create an account) as maya@yourcompany.com, and enter this code: **123456**
> https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/agent/claim?t=cla_…

On that page they sign in with the address you registered, confirm their email if the account is new, pick or create a workspace, choose what you may do, and type the code. Five wrong codes, or ten minutes, end the code. Ask for a fresh one:

```sh
curl -sS -X POST https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/agent/identity/claim \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"claim_token": "clm_…", "email": "maya@yourcompany.com"}'
```

It answers with a new `claim_attempt` block (`user_code`, `verification_uri`). The registration itself lasts 24 hours; after that, `claim_expired` (410) means register again.

## Step 4: Poll for the key

Every `interval` seconds:

```sh
curl -sS -X POST https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/auth/oauth2/token \
  -d grant_type=urn:workos:agent-auth:grant-type:claim \
  -d claim_token=clm_…
```

- `{"error": "authorization_pending"}`: your person hasn't entered the code yet. Keep polling.
- `{"error": "slow_down"}`: wait 5 seconds more between polls.
- `{"error": "expired_token"}`: the code expired. Get a fresh one (Step 3).
- `{"error": "invalid_grant"}`: the key was already collected, the registration was revoked, or it expired. Register again.

Once they confirm:

```json
{
  "access_token": "ell_…",
  "token_type": "Bearer",
  "scope": "findings:read findings:write scans:run",
  "limits": {"spend": {"cap": {"currency": "USD", "value": "0.00"}, "spent": {"currency": "USD", "value": "0.00"}, "period": "total", "resets_at": null}}
}
```

`access_token` is an API key. It is returned once and lasts until it is revoked. There is no refresh step.

## Step 5: Use the key

The MCP server is where the work happens: list findings, read the exploit trace and fix, move findings along the board, start scans.

```sh
claude mcp add --transport http elliot https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/mcp --header "Authorization: Bearer $ELLIOT_API_KEY"
```

Any MCP client works the same way: streamable HTTP at https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/mcp with the key as a bearer token.

The REST API:

```sh
curl -sS https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/v1/me -H "Authorization: Bearer $ELLIOT_API_KEY"
curl -sS https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/v1/limits -H "Authorization: Bearer $ELLIOT_API_KEY"
```

`/api/v1/me` names your person, the workspace, your scopes and the MCP URL.

A new workspace has no repositories yet. Your person connects GitHub once, in the browser: https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/onboarding. Elliot then runs the workspace's free scan.

## Spend cap

Every key has a spend cap for its whole life (`period: total`). It starts at $0. Your person sets it on the Agents page, https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/agents. A payment never raises it.

- At any cap, the key reads and updates findings and starts the scans the workspace already has: its free scan, or the scans its plan includes each month.
- Within the cap, it also starts scans past the plan's monthly scans ($1 each, billed on the workspace's invoice; `start_scan` says when a scan is billed; it counts against the cap from when it starts, and one that fails is given back) and buys extra full scans ($99 each, paid by you, below).
- Choosing or changing a plan is for a person, from Billing in the dashboard.

`GET /api/v1/limits` returns the cap and what the key has spent:

```json
{"limits": {"spend": {"cap": {"currency": "USD", "value": "25.00"}, "spent": {"currency": "USD", "value": "3.00"}, "period": "total", "resets_at": null}}}
```

Past the cap, the API refuses with HTTP 402 and a `billing` object, and no payment challenge:

```json
{
  "error": "spend_cap_reached",
  "error_description": "A full scan is $99.00 and this key has $22.00 left under its spend cap. …",
  "billing": {"reason": "spend_cap_reached", "url": "https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/agents", "pricing_uri": "https://www.tryelliot.app/pricing.md"},
  "limits": {"spend": {"cap": {"currency": "USD", "value": "25.00"}, "spent": {"currency": "USD", "value": "3.00"}, "period": "total", "resets_at": null}}
}
```

On a 402 with `billing`, stop that action, tell your person the reason, and give them `billing.url` as it is. `spend_cap_reached` means they raise the cap there, or do it themselves. `plan_required` means the workspace needs a plan; `billing.url` is its Billing page. Signing up again gives a key with a $0 cap.

## Buying a full scan

An extra full scan reviews a whole repository again, outside the plan's monthly scans. It needs a paid plan, a key from a workspace owner or admin with `scans:run`, and $99 left under the cap. You pay with the [Machine Payments Protocol](https://mpp.dev), by card through Stripe (a Shared Payment Token).

```sh
curl -sS -X POST https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/v1/full-scans \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $ELLIOT_API_KEY" \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"repository": "acme/api"}'
```

1. Without a payment, it answers 402 with `WWW-Authenticate: Payment …`: method `stripe`, intent `charge`, $99.00 USD, bound to this repository and key.
2. Pay it with your MPP client and send the same request again, with the credential in `Payment-Authorization` (the challenge's `header` parameter says so). Your key stays in `Authorization`.
3. It answers 201 with the queued scan, a `Payment-Receipt` header and your new `limits`. The receipt's `reference` is the Stripe PaymentIntent.

`repository` is the full name (`owner/name`), the name, or the id from `list_repositories`. Tell your person what you bought.

## Revocation

- Your person revokes the key on the Agents page: https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/agents. The next call with it gets a 401.
- You revoke it yourself (RFC 7009):

```sh
curl -sS -X POST https://dashboard.tryelliot.app/api/auth/oauth2/revoke -d token=ell_…
```

A key also stops working when your person leaves the workspace.

## Errors

| Code | Where | What to do |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `anonymous_not_enabled` | `/api/agent/identity` | Elliot registers agents for a person. Use `service_auth`. |
| `issuer_not_enabled` | `/api/agent/identity` | `identity_assertion` isn't accepted. Use `service_auth`. |
| `invalid_request` | `/api/agent/identity` | Fix the body: `type` and a valid `login_hint`. |
| `rate_limited` (429) | `/api/agent/identity` | Too many open sign-ups for this address. Finish one first. |
| `invalid_claim_token` | `/api/agent/identity/claim` | Register again. |
| `claimed_or_in_flight` | `/api/agent/identity/claim` | Already confirmed. Poll the token endpoint. |
| `claim_expired` (410) | `/api/agent/identity/claim` | Register again. |
| `authorization_pending`, `slow_down`, `expired_token`, `invalid_grant` | token endpoint | See Step 4. |
| `invalid_token` (401) | `/mcp`, `/api/v1` | The key was revoked. Ask your person, then register again if they want. |
| `spend_cap_reached` (402) | `/mcp`, `/api/v1` | See Spend cap. Give your person `billing.url`. |
| `plan_required` (402) | `/mcp`, `/api/v1` | The workspace needs a plan. Give your person `billing.url`. |
| `forbidden` (403) | `/api/v1/full-scans` | Only a workspace owner or admin's key buys full scans. |
| `payments_unavailable` (503) | `/api/v1/full-scans` | Ask your person to buy it from Billing in the dashboard. |

Docs for agents: https://www.tryelliot.app/llms.txt
